{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789503387,"nonce":"YXmbSoe0e0yP+06uxcYCgi7dxr4=","title":"tokenize: a str key is boxed, copied and hashed twice per counting statement","message":"bench_tokenize's counting loop, `for tok in text.split(\" \"): counts[tok] = counts.get(tok, 0) + 1`, is the kernel's largest phase and the whole of its loss to PyPy: 300,000 iterations in 35 ms on the M1 Pro (117 ns each; 50 ms when a collection lands inside it) against PyPy's 19 ms, on a kernel PyPy finishes in 60 ms wall to zypy's 90.\n\nPer iteration the lowering makes five allocations where PyPy makes one: `tok` is a str element of the split list, so each of its two uses as a dict key copies the string into a fresh box (`zb_str_to_dynamic`: a string copy and a box), each fresh box is hashed from scratch and compared by content (the stored key is a different pointer), and the count is boxed once it passes the interned range. The get's box is released after the call now that the lookups borrow their key; the set's box is dropped inside `zb_dict_set` when the key was already present, and the value it replaces with it, both left to the collector. A sample of the loop with the collector off: 26% in allocation and string copying, 17% in `string_hash`, `string_equals` and memcmp, 10% in the thread-local lookup inside `zyntax_alloc`/`zyntax_free` (seven per iteration), the rest the inlined probing.\n\nDirections, in order of reach: (1) a str local boxed for a dynamic use is boxed once per statement and the box reused by the later uses, so the get borrows and the set keeps the same box (one copy, one hash, cached in the box after the first lookup); (2) a subscript store whose key the same statement just looked up in the same dict, with nothing between that could change the dict, stores at the found position instead of probing again, and only an absent key goes through the insert; (3) `zb_dict_set` hands back the key it did not keep so an owned box can be released at the call site instead of collected. With the split list's elements boxed once at the head of the loop body, (1) also covers every use of the loop variable.","files":null}]}